cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the scPASU paper listed
  under preferred-citation below.
title: >-
  scPASU: a pipeline to repurpose scRNA-seq data for single cell
  polyadenylation analysis
abstract: >-
  Original source repository for scPASU, a pipeline that repurposes
  3' scRNA-seq data for alternative polyadenylation analysis by
  generating a dataset-specific poly(A) site reference. Developed
  2022-2023 at the Lerner Research Institute, Cleveland Clinic.
  This repository is the source from which the release accompanying
  the publication (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14498599) was
  derived.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Surbhi
  - family-names: Sona
  - orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6644-8970" 
  - affiliation: "Lerner Research Institute, Cleveland Clinic"
  - current affiliation: St Jude Children's Hospital 
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-10"                          
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/2019surbhi/scPASU"
keywords:
  - alternative polyadenylation
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - poly(A) site usage
  - bioinformatics
  - APA

